%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b360da9bf94d30246b40adae73f848a5, type: 3}
  m_Name: TutorialDatabase
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::TutorialDatabase
  tutorials:
  - id: T_SHOPPING
    triggerFlag: tutorial.shopping_available
    behaviourId: Shopping
    priority: 80
    activationPhase: Market
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.shopping_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: shop
      text: Welcome to your bistro! First, shop for today's cooking. Open Recipes
        in the top bar to see what each dish needs, then drag food from the shelves
        into your cart. Buy enough for at least one recipe, then check out.
  - id: T_SORTING
    triggerFlag: tutorial.sorting_available
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 90
    activationPhase: FoodSorting
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.sorting_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: Sort each new food into Green, Yellow or Red. Green foods are the everyday
        foundation and the only foods that build health. Yellow foods are ones customers
        are moving away from. Red foods are the ones to avoid. Flip a card to read
        its ingredients. Each new food you sort correctly gives back {maxDiscount}
        of what you paid for it. Answers are final once you submit.
  - id: T_COOKING
    triggerFlag: tutorial.cooking_available
    behaviourId: FirstMeal
    priority: 70
    activationPhase: Service
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.cooking_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: choose
      text: Time to cook! Pick a recipe you have ingredients for. Faded recipes are
        missing something.
    - stepId: build
      text: Drag one serving at a time from your pantry into the recipe's slots.
        A red outline means a slot still needs something. Drag a row out of a slot
        to put it back. For your first dish, fill every slot exactly, then press
        Review dish.
    - stepId: feedback
      text: 'Your first dish is done! You used {ingredients}. Health changed by {healthDelta},
        and it covered these Daily Dozen groups: {dailyDozen}. Only Green foods build
        health. Each Daily Dozen group a guest hasn''t had before adds a little extra,
        so vary the plants you serve. From now on, you can also serve dishes that
        don''t match the recipe, but guests will notice.'
  - id: T_CRASH
    triggerFlag: tutorial.first_crash_dialogue_completed
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 100
    activationPhase: Service
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.rush_crash_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: That guest felt a quick burst of energy, then a slump. A rush can feel
        good in the moment, but it doesn't mean the meal was good for them. Judge
        a meal by what's in it, not by how lively a guest seems afterwards.
  - id: T_RENT
    triggerFlag: tutorial.rent_upcoming
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 95
    activationPhase: Market
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.rent_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: 'A letter from the landlord: from tomorrow, rent of ${rent} is due every
        morning. You can only shop while you have money, so keep a little cushion.
        Busy evenings bring in takeaway income, and guests will soon start arriving
        with requests.'
  - id: T_SELL
    triggerFlag: tutorial.money_low
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 96
    activationPhase: Market
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.sell_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: Money is running low, and tomorrow's rent could leave you unable to shop.
        Open Pantry, drag food you won't use onto SELL, then press Sell. Food that
        would spoil before you cook it is the best thing to sell.
  - id: T_REQUESTS
    triggerFlag: okinawa_chef_arrived
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 85
    activationPhase: Service
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.requests_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: From today, guests may ask for something, like Savory, Creamy or Crunchy.
        Each recipe shows what it answers. Answering a request delights a guest and
        grows your popularity; ignoring it costs a little. Health still comes only
        from the foods you choose. Comfort is answered by any dish with an appeal
        of {comfort} or more.
  - id: T_FARMER
    triggerFlag: tutorial.food_aid_given
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 99
    activationPhase: Service
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.farmer_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: Your pantry couldn't make any recipe, so a local farmer brought a small
        crate of plain staples, enough for one simple dish. The farmer can only help
        once a day, so shop or sell spare food to get back on your feet.
  - id: T_DAY
    triggerFlag: tutorial.toolbar_day
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 110
    activationPhase: Any
    completionFlags: []
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: 'You have {totalDays} days to make your bistro''s name. Each day: shop,
        sort what''s new, then cook for your guests. Rent starts on day {rentStart},
        and guests bring requests from day {cravingsStart}. At the end, your popularity
        and the community''s wellbeing decide how the story ends.'
  - id: T_POPULARITY
    triggerFlag: tutorial.toolbar_popularity
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 110
    activationPhase: Any
    completionFlags: []
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: Popularity is how well known your bistro is. More guests come at {guestThresholds}
        popularity (up to {maxGuests}), and above {walkInThreshold}, walk-in customers
        buy takeaway every evening. Delighted guests, answered requests and tasty
        plates raise it; mismatched dishes and ignored requests lower it.
  - id: T_WALLET
    triggerFlag: tutorial.toolbar_wallet
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 110
    activationPhase: Any
    completionFlags: []
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: Guests pay you, plus tips, for every dish, and the market takes your
        money for food. From day {rentStart}, rent of ${rent} is due each morning.
        You can only shop while you have money, and ending deep in debt closes the
        bistro. Short on cash? Sell spare food from the Pantry.
  fingerprint: X90rd7/R9tEcSkgq8zNBK/oGQdh2Mm1j+R6DgtlDZ1s=
